WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.190 --> 00:00:00.980
The Admiral: Okay.

2
00:00:01.540 --> 00:00:06.920
The Admiral: Well, I'm sorry that we got started half an hour late then, But still, cool.

3
00:00:07.820 --> 00:00:11.329
The Admiral: Previously on Barkwin Teen.

4
00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:12.500
The Captain: -Oh.

5
00:00:13.150 --> 00:00:15.600
The Admiral: The infection spread.

6
00:00:16.030 --> 00:00:35.789
The Admiral: What began as angry red welts on room and the captain bloomed into something worse. Pulsing patches that throbbed in time with your heartbeats. Healing magic slides off like oil. Dispel magic does nothing. The thing inside your veins is awake, and it's testing the walls.

7
00:00:36.520 --> 00:00:47.770
The Admiral: In the strange, timeless drift of the astral plane, where thought itself can move you and sounds arrive before their makers, you had one short day to search for answers.

8
00:00:47.880 --> 00:00:49.860
The Admiral: One day before the flotilla.

9
00:00:50.200 --> 00:00:55.800
The Admiral: And an unknown day before whatever's growing inside decides to bring itself to the surface.

10
00:00:56.970 --> 00:01:16.040
The Admiral: Room tried everything he could, from protection from poison, and greater restoration, but the marks only darkened and the ache only deepened. The captain sought wisdom from Elder Abarrett, and though no help, he spoke of names and heraldry, gifting the captain with a gift-sized mask to wear when phasing his people.

11
00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:22.929
The Admiral: Not as a conquering hero, But as a mysterious and nameless captain sliding into the flotilla.

12
00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:27.830
The Admiral: It was Lumi who ventured into stranger waters.

13
00:01:28.300 --> 00:01:34.479
The Admiral: Twice he's spoken the words vile darkness, and twice the shadow entity appeared.

14
00:01:34.820 --> 00:01:40.299
The Admiral: First reading from its Book of Smoke and Ash, revealing cryptic truths.

15
00:01:40.750 --> 00:01:52.039
The Admiral: Then, through the Divine Spell… then, later, through the Divine Spell Commune, reaching out to his mom, watching from beyond. Three questions he posed.

16
00:01:52.300 --> 00:01:55.929
The Admiral: Is there anyone currently on the ship who knows how to cure us? No.

17
00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:01.930
The Admiral: will reach the flotilla before they're taken over by the infection? Unclear.

18
00:02:03.120 --> 00:02:05.290
The Admiral: Is my father Vecna?

19
00:02:05.780 --> 00:02:11.300
The Admiral: No Her visage fading, the infection spreading.

20
00:02:11.470 --> 00:02:18.789
The Admiral: And through the silvery void we see it. Not a star, but a small planet of ships, the Gif Flotilla.

21
00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:23.320
The Admiral: An astral fortress of hundreds of thousands of vessels.

22
00:02:23.630 --> 00:02:31.229
The Admiral: Layered and spread in three dimensions, bristling with cannons and standards, the thunder of distant artillery.

23
00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:40.699
The Admiral: At its heart, the great flagships. At its edges, repair yards, mess halls, patrol craft, and vendors from countless worlds beyond.

24
00:02:40.830 --> 00:02:45.020
The Admiral: An entire civilization drifting through the Astral Sea as one.

25
00:02:45.930 --> 00:02:58.050
The Admiral: It's the largest gathering of gifts in centuries. A city of mercenaries and soldiers, glory and judgment. And somewhere, deep within the maze of steel, plank, and canvas, someone…

26
00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.010
The Admiral: Who might be able to save you?

